Unexpected PDF generation error

Authorization

@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard) with @Roles('MEMBER'). The identity (memberId) is strictly inferred from @CurrentUser() linking to the members table. A member cannot request another member's statement.

Input Validation

startDate and endDate: Must be valid dates, and endDate must be ≥ startDate.

Flow

Authenticate request and verify MEMBER role.

Resolve memberId from the authenticated userId.

Fetch chronological timeline using TransactionRepository.getMemberTimeline(memberId, dates).

Calculate a running balance (credits - charges) over the timeline.

If format === 'pdf', utilize ExportService to write the header, member details, tabular transaction rows, and closing balance into a PDF buffer.

Return JSON or stream the PDF buffer.

Acceptance Criteria

Endpoint & Logic

 Returns 200 with chronological transaction history.

 Correctly calculates opening and closing running balances.

 Returns a valid PDF binary stream when format=pdf.

Authorization

 ADMIN role is denied (403) — Admins have Reports (Sprint 10); this is strictly a Member feature.

 Request parameters cannot specify a memberId; identity is locked to the JWT.

Code Quality

 PDF generation reuses the ExportService from Sprint 10 rather than reinventing a local PDF generator.

 No linting errors or warnings.

Dependencies

IKM-8.1 (Unified Ledger), IKM-10.1 (ExportService)
